# What goes in the SDIST — deliberately NOT the wheel.
#
# The wheel is code only: `tests/test_packaging_contents.py` asserts it contains zero
# non-.py entries outside dist-info. MANIFEST.in cannot add files to a wheel
# built by setuptools without `include_package_data`, which is exactly why it is the right
# tool here — it makes the source distribution complete (a contributor can `pip download
# --no-binary` and get a runnable checkout with the suites and the test suite) while
# leaving the installed program untouched.
graft examples
graft docs
graft tests
# MP-100: `graft tests` without this shipped a suite that cannot import itself -- [M] an
# unpacked sdist collected 2 errors, `No module named 'scripts'`, because
# tests/test_recall_arm.py and tests/test_fp_measurement_repertoire.py do
# `from scripts.fp_measurement import ...`. It is not only the tests: the Drift Map's own
# published reproduce command is `python scripts/drift_map.py`, and README links
# scripts/fp_measurement.py. Enforced by test_packaging_contents.py, which now runs
# `pytest --collect-only` INSIDE the unpacked sdist -- a name list cannot see this.
graft scripts
# MP-203: `action.yml` (the root manifest) was `include`d but `actions/` -- which holds the
# Action's own detailed docs, `actions/README.md` -- was not, and `.github/` was absent
# entirely. [M] 2026-09-07: an sdist installed exactly as CONTRIBUTING.md instructs failed
# **3** tests, from TWO missing directories:
#   .github/  -> test_config.py, test_first_run_cost.py  (2 tests)
#   actions/  -> test_exit_code_contract.py             (1 test)
# The repo's own suite can never catch this: it runs inside the git checkout, where both
# directories always exist. Only `pytest` INSIDE an unpacked sdist occupies that state --
# which is why `test_packaging_contents.py` runs one.
#
# Only `actions/` is grafted. `.github/` is deliberately NOT: it is a dot-directory, and
# `test_sdist_excludes_private_directories` forbids every hidden path from a distribution
# that, unlike the repo, is published. The two tests that read it are REPO-HYGIENE checks
# ("does the dogfood workflow point at the right config") which are meaningless in an
# installed sdist, so they skip when it is absent rather than being paid for in shipped
# bytes. `actions/README.md` is different in kind -- published documentation of the Action's
# own output contract, which the sdist claims to be a complete checkout of.
graft actions
include data/models.json
include CONTRIBUTING.md CHANGELOG.md SECURITY.md CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
include action.yml
prune ops
prune .claude
prune reports
global-exclude *.pyc __pycache__/*
